avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T11:06:09-08:00","id":1527858,"title":"","content":"So finally had some free time and finished the Apocryphals + Spoken. I will probably take some time at adding some homebrew Exalts into the timeline before dealing with the canon Exigents in terms of mechanis and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T17:19:19-08:00","id":1528854,"title":"","content":"Finally finished all of the Canon + Apocryphal + Exigents with mechanics writeups- now I can start with the homebrew Exalts which were described in the timeline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T21:28:59-08:00","id":1528984,"title":"","content":"With Across the Eight Directions out, I wonder if the Spiral of Aiun is the kind of thing Xiwangmu creates, or if that is an aspect of Cajerron that Aiun awoke and remade into a cosmic guardian of her continent...and now that she's gone, it's instinctively trying to recreate Cajerron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T05:32:57-08:00","id":1529001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1525996-modified-exalted-setting?p=1528984#post1528984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Across the Eight Directions out, I wonder if the Spiral of Aiun is the kind of thing Xiwangmu creates, or if that is an aspect of Cajerron that Aiun awoke and remade into a cosmic guardian of her continent...and now that she's gone, it's instinctively trying to recreate Cajerron.</div> </div> </div> </div>Xiwangmu (as currently perceived) is found in Hell so she is less likely to be the culprit- but the Spiral could be a interesting way to integrate Cybele and Cajerron's shards. I might through something about this to the Tellurian's upcoming writeup, so thanks for pointing it out!<br /> <br /> Also, in general At8D is full of strange stuff that I think would be very could to use for this project- I already have plans for the dying heart under the frozen plains of the Northwest and the Azurite's Sea Courts among others, as well as the source of constant plagues that comes from the Northeast. A lot of cool ideas to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T15:08:58-08:00","id":1529040,"title":"","content":"&quot;Nebiru, the guardian of the invisible planet, fearing the cost of Exaltation and believing that the gods will lose the coming <i><b>wart</b>,&quot; </i>Emphasis mine<br /> I know it is a minor typo, but it twigs me every time.<br /> <br /> Edit: Okay, I really like the <b>Tellurians</b>. My favourite original addition so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 01-20-2024, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T06:57:11-08:00","id":1529302,"title":"","content":"Finished the three homebrew Chosen of a Greater Incarna Patrons. Next would probably be the Chosen of the Lesser Incrana, which would probably modify the setting to a more significant degree. Also, as this is a pretty big document, it is hard for me to notice all of the different typos which I write in it, so if anyone who is already reading the document want to help in correcting those contact me through a PM and I would give you commenting access <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (also, if someone actually wants to contribute more actively to the project in terms of developing those concepts, feel free to talk to me as well! I won't say no to another pair of writing hands :P)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T16:00:14-08:00","id":1529738,"title":"","content":"So I finished integrating the Lesser Incrana and their Chosen to the setting's timeline (full writeups are still in the To Do list).<br /> <br /> Now, I feel like I need to detail a bit what exactly I have been doing with the Lesser Incrana- originally, the idea of them was using it as a blanket term for &quot;less powerful Incrana which are also less known&quot;, a way to integrate a few new Exalts with minimal disruption to the setting. Basically, all of the Incrana were to have the same esoteric origin, with the Lesser ones simply being less powerful gods, somewhat on par with the patrons of Terrestrial Exaltations such as the Dark Mother, the Elemental Dragons or Ketu. However, as I started on working on them, something felt a bit &quot;off&quot; about the attitude- sure, it could have worked, but the whole metaphysical shenanigans which are going in the setting have started to feel stretched- if all Incrana are just the same type of being, why the magical materials which the Lesser Incrana are tied to are less important? Also, why to have seven of them? What makes Hemera, the Goddess of Day's Sky, less important than, let's say, Nox or the Maidens? Why Iris, the Goddess of the Rainbows, have avoided making Exalts during the Primordial War? Why Neith and Ouranos were significantly weaker compared to the true Incrana? Basically- if not all Incrana were made equal, why were they made at all?<br /> <br /> So I was watching Hazbin Hotel while I was thinking about the subject, and then I was struck by an idea- in the Hellaverse, you have numerous demonic hierarchies, with the Royal Family and Seven Sins standing at the top. Below them, however, are the Goetia (Hell's nobility), and then the Overlords, those mortal souls which were doomed to Hell, yet through clever use of deals they have managed to grow in power and influence. However, as strong as they might be, even the power of the strongest of Overlords will be lesser compared to the Goetia, not to mention the Sins, as they have the inborn right to rule Hell. In a way, the Goetia are <i>made</i> to rule Hell, while the Overlords have to <i>earn</i> them, and what other entity do we know about that has to earn their power and position through bureaucratic systems? Why, the gods of Exalted of course!<br /> <br /> After all, in Exalted, gods gain most of their metaphysical substance from their job in the Celestial Bureaucracy. It determines their power and influence, and shapes their form and rituals. As such, this could make an interesting point- for while the Incrana were made to be the greatest gods in Creation, governing the most important aspects of reality, what if some gods, through acts of heroism and cunning, have also managed to gain the favor of the ancients (or the Incrana), and gain a position of comparable power? Sure, they won't reach the same power level of the Incrana (there is a glass ceiling after all), but they could reach something very close to it, becoming something like the Incrana, yet still lesser compared to them. Actual Lesser Incrana.<br /> <br /> Sure, this idea is obviously not for everyone, but hey this is an Apocryphal Setting so I can do whatever I want :P After all, with such a legendary status being a possibility, I could imagine it would affect how gods interact with one another, attempting to gain the favor of the Incrana as they aspire to be accepted as one of them, something that only happened once after the Divine Revolution, sure, but hey Ahlat can dream, right? And with that in mind, I started developing the gods who have managed to gain this aspired state- Ouranos, the old Plaguebearer who got governance over a dying star for inventing diseases as a method of population control, the Mysteries, the emissaries to other worlds who made deals with the titans to reach their status, Neith, who have captured the twin hearts of the Empyreal Chaos through song and dance and was crowned by a far star, Andromeda, who gained power over the dark shadow which eats the light of stars in Heavens after orchestrating a betrayal by the race which worshiped her towards the Great Maker- only to betray them instead, Polaris, a proto-goddess who reached out of Zen Mu to guide Creation with her stable Pole Star, Hemera, who fought alongside the Sun in the failed world of Cajerron and got the honor of governing the Celestial Dome, and Iris, the daughter of the fallen Aurora who was promoted to fill the void he left behind after the war, only to sacrifice herself after Balor almost destroyed Creation.<br /> <br /> So yeah, this idea might not be for everyone, and if you dislike it yet still want to have those Incrana and their Chosen as part of the game, you can just assume that they, indeed, were just Incrana with less mojo to them due to the circumstances of their Creation. I still like this idea, and I hope you too would at least find it of interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T15:52:17-08:00","id":1529776,"title":"","content":"So somehow I managed to cross the 100 pages in this project, and now the Google Docs started to be all clunky and annoying, constantly shutting down my browser as it takes forever to load. As we are still not even halfway through this project, I have decided to break apart the whole Doc into different sections, putting the link to each of the sections in the original Doc. This certainly makes my life easier :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-17T15:42:38-08:00","id":1531037,"title":"","content":"So while I'm working on the Chosen of the Lesser Incrana (almost finished those guys, just two more), I've added a new sub-project in this already way too large of a writing project- Protocol: IMMACULACY. Basically, a Exalted shard which combines concepts from Shadowrun/SCP Foundation/Fate, creating a cyberpunk setting ruled by shadow conspiracies who use ancient rituals based around their mystical icons in order to summon heroic power upon Chosen individuals, and that can only by contained by the efforts of the Protocol. This one is going to be on a smaller fire for now, as I have more important things to finish beforehand (like the politics section, or, you know, <i>the rest of the bloody Chosen</i>).<br /> <br /> God I spend too much time on this project for no good reason other than ideas just buzzing in my head... -_-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-21T15:11:55-08:00","id":1531254,"title":"","content":"Finished the politics section for all existing Exalts. Now, just to find time to deal with the Bow Bearers...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T15:27:47-08:00","id":1531311,"title":"","content":"Aaaand finally I finished with the Bow Bearers. Might take a break before moving the to Primordial Exalts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T01:17:00-08:00","id":1531498,"title":"","content":"I'm really enjoying your ideas and takes on the setting overall. My only real complaint is your persistent misspelling of &quot;Incarna&quot; as &quot;Incrana.&quot; XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T13:24:30-08:00","id":1531538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackwingedheaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1525996-modified-exalted-setting?p=1531498#post1531498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really enjoying your ideas and takes on the setting overall. My only real complaint is your persistent misspelling of &quot;Incarna&quot; as &quot;Incrana.&quot; XD</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll never manage to correctly spell this word :P I'll try to keep attention to it, but I make no promises (as I said before, if someone wants to help with editing spelling and grammar or more, feel free to approach, but I lack the mental capability to read through it all)<br /> <br /> But anyway, I'm happy to hear you enjoy the project!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T17:02:01-08:00","id":1531820,"title":"","content":"And finally, I have finished integrating the Primordial Exalts to the History section (not their full writeups for the project), as well as a few Eras from the different artifacts sections (and some other modifications for other sections as well).<br /> <br /> I must say that those Exalts somewhat gave more more headache than the Celestial Exalts. I mean, previously I could just made up a whole new Incarna, killing them off and then work on some fictional history. However, the Primordial Exalts were more complicated because, well, the primordials generally <i>didn't</i> made Chosen. Sure, there are a few canon outliners (Autochthon, Sacheverell and Oramus), but the vast majority, as it seems, either didn't knew how to do so or didn't want to due to the circumstances. While I have added some &quot;original cast&quot;, there is a limit to how many primordials I can make up before it feels weird, and there are themes which I want to explore for existing ones, hence me going through an headache that every time I decided on a new patron, I had to think about both how did they learn the way to create Exalts, why they did so, and how they did it when they are either dead, gone or bound by the surrender oaths. Still, I think I did do my best.<br /> <br /> Among the homebrew primordials, we had 2 which were pretty original and one which was adapted from the Memorial Exalted project. Sedna was a very easy choice for me- the idea of the Glacials as the Chosen of a primordial related to cold who have escaped Creation during the Primordial War was one of the first ideas that came to my mind long, long, <i>long</i> time ago (basically when I became aware of Exalted for the first time). The reason is that ever since I was a child, I was obsessed with &quot;Winter-based&quot; fantasy forces, probably because of how the Snow Queen was my favorite fairytale. As such, I found it very easy to adapt Sedna, a goddess related to the arctic irl and the name of a dwarf planet found deep in the Kuiper belt (hence the name) to the setting as one of the primordials who have lurked beyond Creation only to invade it later. Things like the Ten Year Winter or the Frozen Star Intrusion from the artifact eras have allowed an easy adaption. You might ask yourself why did I used Sedna and not Hunanura, which was implied to be a primordial related to cold in 2e, but I wanted to use Sedna for the astronomical reference and, well, Hunanura was dead in 2e, so you may consider it as a behemoth created by Sedna or something in this setting. Relating her to the dying thing which sleeps in the Northwest was just a fun little easter egg. I still need to think about what did the Glacials actually did in Creation, but I guess I will develop it later.<br /> <br /> As for the other two, Thalassa was pretty much made as a neutral primordial as reference for how in greek mythology the sea took a neutral stance in the Titanomachy, while also serving as the patron of the Chosen of the Depths- the ide for a new Exalt splat which was discarded early on. Still, I like the idea, so it is going to show up here- I originally considered them to be present across the time of Creation, but while thinking about possible history for them I eventually decided that with Primordial Exaltation taking the form of a &quot;process&quot; rather than an &quot;object&quot;, it would be interesting for the process to be forgotten after the Niobraran War due to all Exalts being killed, only for it to resurface a millennia later. Mnemosyne, on the other hand, have been mostly the same as in her presentation in the Memorials project- she is the primordial who invented the idea of death and drew the Underworld for Creation, and which sided with the gods in the War, creating her own Chosen. I have changed the circumstances behind her death, however, with her getting killed by the Neverborn while trying to create a process for their reincarnation. Still probably need to expand on the actual history of the Chroniclers, as the Memorials are called in this setting.<br /> <br /> This gave me (when Autochthon is included) 4 types of Exalts, which meant that I needed at least 5 more to complete the &quot;set&quot;. For this, I have turned to canon primordials. Gaia was a very intuitive choice, as people have talked a lot about the possibility for her having Chosen of her own. While I considered to do something else, in the end I decided to stop beting around the bush, as the Animal Avatars were implied a lot to be &quot;Gaia's answer for the Exalts only in animal form&quot;, so I decided to just role with it. I am yet to decide whether or not those animals with a human soul would have a human or animal body (I am wary of using shapeshifting due to Lunars being a thing), but regardless, I think it is a good way to integrate those guys. The more &quot;druidic&quot; aesthetic was instead taken by the Arcadians, the Chosen of Cytherea- which is something I like because I really wanted to do something with her, and her Chosen masquerading as the Gaian Exalts feels appropriate (and it was implied in 2e that she has some connection to dragon lines, so we are going to play around with that part). Isidoros was also a easy choice- after all, originally he was supposed to have Chosen of his own, like Oramus and Sacheverell. The Unfettered, however, are going to be somewhat different from the Revelers, but I may try to draw inspiration from them to a degree. I have also considered Ramethus (hence why you would see references for him in the writeup), but eventually I decided to give him a different role.<br /> <br /> Now we are going to the more difficult choices- SWLiHN was chosen simply because I read somewhere that someone had an ide for her having Chosen with insect like aesthetic, and because the Three Spheres Cataclysm felt like a naturally way to introduce an instant for Exaltation. Surprisingly, while I started thinking about her Exalts, the more I started to &quot;get&quot; their fictional history, creating the Burning Pyre Empire in order to integrate them (something I pretty much like). Szorny was not the first Choice for me as a candidate for Exaltation, but I do like this Yozi and I did originally used him as a catalyst for the corrupted version of the Lunar Exalts, so while it took me a while to think how did he found out the secret of Exaltation and why it would use it, eventually I managed to piece it out together (not to mention that having the Silver Forest teaching Isidoros how to make Chosen and Isidoros just rolling with it while Szorny taking his time just felt appropriate). Using Ta'akozoka for the Yearned, however, was something that I had in mind from the beginning of this project- in the original draft, his Chosen were some kind of corrupted Lunars, yet in this iteration he made ones by himself. Him doing so as a Neverborn was not a easy choice to make, but considered that according to many fan writeups Ta'akozoka is one of the primordials to favor Necromancy it made sense that he would keep a sense of lucidity compared to the other Neverborn, something which would allow him to play around in Creation and eventually make Exalts of his own- sacrificing that lucidity as a toll for the act.<br /> <br /> Now, this should have been enough Exalts for the Primordials, but the thing was that there were some candidates that I wanted to integrate and simply didn't had a room for them. While I considered a state similar to the one I used for the Celestials (one set which resonates with the primary MM from the family and one with the secondary), I didn't had enough ideas for a whole new set, and the project is bloated as is so I need to trim where possible. This is where I decided to introduce five more patrons which represent the primary colours of jade, as none of the Exalts actually resonates with it (sure, the Gnostics resonate with yilistr, but it is not the same thing), and it would help to reinforce each of the colours as its own MM. The main figure which I wanted to adapt was, actually, Jheel Khan- I was always interested in this primordial, and with the description of Vainglory it felt appropriate to use her as the power behind it. There is a note that unlike Ta'akozoka, the Accursed are not truly the Chosen of the Neverborn which Jheel Khan became, but were created from the last remnant of her living Essence through her jeweled blood, which was later cursed by her own ghost. The Sophists were another idea which I made up for the original project and which I really liked, so integrating them was a fun experience. Kimbery having her own Chosen felt almost natural, even though that the whole Lintha spin around their Exalts put some challenged in order to adapt how her Chosen came into being. The Withered were actually a mishmash of different concepts that I had, with Metagaos being &quot;draconic&quot; felt like a good enough reason to use him as a patron for a Jade related Exalts. Finally, the Ebon Dragon was the most difficult choice I made for a patron, one of which I am yet to feel completely comfortable with. However, using his Exalts in order to integrate lore from 2e Infernals (in terms of them being a &quot;secret spy org&quot; and some pieces from the RotSE) felt like a fun experience. Oh, and if you ask yourself &quot;how did Jheel Khan and Ta'akozoka got Exalts while Mardukth didn't when he is the most well known Neverborn in 2e&quot;, don't worry, he is around- just in a different section of the project.<br /> <br /> So yeah, this is a comprehensive reasoning for why each of the primordials was chosen as patrons for this project. Hope you find it of interest while I start working on the writeup for the Exalts themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T16:31:01-08:00","id":1532263,"title":"","content":"Just noting that I returned from my break and finished the first of the homebrew Primordial Exalts- the Glacials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T09:25:58-07:00","id":1536367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1525996-modified-exalted-setting?p=1528984#post1528984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Across the Eight Directions out, I wonder if the Spiral of Aiun is the kind of thing Xiwangmu creates, or if that is an aspect of Cajerron that Aiun awoke and remade into a cosmic guardian of her continent...and now that she's gone, it's instinctively trying to recreate Cajerron.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just started reading on the Isles of Aiun and Junji Ito's <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qRrqvjjKlOs\" target=\"_blank\">Uzumaki</a> vibes came out strong when reading on the Spiral and its influence.<br /> Whatever it is in nature, deity, demon, deva, elemental, fae, behemoth, something else, no clues at all though in power it stands somewhere between 2nd and 3rd circle demon for certain.<br /> <br /> <br /> edit: Whirlpools, tornadoes, <b><i>typhoons</i></b>.... phantasms, hallucinations, <i><b>nightmares</b></i>.... Maybe the Spiral is not as unknowable as it may at first seem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-27-2024, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T19:35:00-07:00","id":1536398,"title":"","content":"OR one could look at things from a different angle - the circumpolar stars could be said to spiral around Polaris in the sky, for example....<br /> <br /> Another hypothesis might be that Aiun inadvertently did not contact but birthed/spawned the Spiral in her attempts to delve into Creation's deepest mysteries through the puisance of the Eye of Autochthon. Ouroboros circles itself in the fashion of the shadows of the elemental dragons' coils.<br /> <br /> Hope i don't derail things too much with my delirious ramblings on the lost isles of Aiun. Got Across the 8 Directions recently, decided to start things with Uiluru &amp; Sovereigns in the Northwest and things just <i>spiraled </i>from there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> But anyway....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1525996-modified-exalted-setting?p=1532263#post1532263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just noting that I returned from my break and finished the first of the homebrew Primordial Exalts- the Glacials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ever considered the possibility of them as a different take on Sovereigns? Crystal &amp; rainbow flame, ice &amp; cold wrath. Magic can persist cold but fluid and roiling under the placid veneer of frost. It would take little to nothing to (re)connect the dots and show the Fount of Glories from a different perspective, imho. Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-28-2024, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T21:12:45-07:00","id":1536399,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1525996-modified-exalted-setting?p=1529738#post1529738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I feel like I need to detail a bit what exactly I have been doing with the Lesser Incrana- originally, the idea of them was using it as a blanket term for &quot;less powerful Incrana which are also less known&quot;, a way to integrate a few new Exalts with minimal disruption to the setting. Basically, all of the Incrana were to have the same esoteric origin, with the Lesser ones simply being less powerful gods, somewhat on par with the patrons of Terrestrial Exaltations such as the Dark Mother, the Elemental Dragons or Ketu. However, as I started on working on them, something felt a bit &quot;off&quot; about the attitude- sure, it could have worked, but the whole metaphysical shenanigans which are going in the setting have started to feel stretched- <i>if all Incrana are just the same type of being, why the magical materials which the Lesser Incrana are tied to are less important? Also, why to have seven of them? What makes Hemera, the Goddess of Day's Sky, less important than, let's say, Nox or the Maidens? Why Iris, the Goddess of the Rainbows, have avoided making Exalts during the Primordial War? Why Neith and Ouranos were significantly weaker compared to the true Incrana</i>? Basically- if not all Incrana were made equal, why were they made at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry if i come off too bluntly, but to me those sound very much chicken &amp; egg dilemmas. Would anyone even think of the Magical Materials as such, instead of forgotten among countless esoteric components/reagents, if there were no Chosen of the Incarnae or Dragons to resonate or disonate with some over others in attempts to draw out evocations out of artifacts made with them? (Not even going into the matter that sometimes those things can go a little pear-shaped, such as Gorgon in Arms of Chosen being made of white jade but <i>also</i> resonating like Soulsteel for those chosen with an affinity for that material - or the matter of white &amp; black jade in general sometimes just going well with things touched by the essence of the Underworld)<br /> <br /> The Incarnae while mysterious and sometimes distant are undeniably still puisant, present and active in Creation's affairs - but how loud is the fall of a tree where nothing exists to hear it? Are the Dark Mother, the Elemental Dragons or Ketu less truly puisant than the UCS, Luna or the Maidens or just more elusive &amp; idiosyncratic on the peculiar priorities in the making of their Chosen? The same principle might be said to apply with any &quot;lesser&quot; Incarna patrons. More obscure/secretive does not exactly have to mean weaker.<br /> <br /> As an aside, i've toyed with the idea of Uranus, Neptune &amp; Pluto as either fallen Maidens - or copycats/impostors entities <b>claiming</b> to be so - in a few past games of my own, among a few other things relating to [alleged] dead Incarnae.\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T10:21:16-07:00","id":1536444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1525996-modified-exalted-setting?p=1536399#post1536399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sorry if i come off too bluntly, but to me those sound very much chicken &amp; egg dilemmas. Would anyone even think of the Magical Materials as such, instead of forgotten among countless esoteric components/reagents, if there were no Chosen of the Incarnae or Dragons to resonate or disonate with some over others in attempts to draw out evocations out of artifacts made with them? (Not even going into the matter that sometimes those things can go a little pear-shaped, such as Gorgon in Arms of Chosen being made of white jade but <i>also</i> resonating like Soulsteel for those chosen with an affinity for that material - or the matter of white &amp; black jade in general sometimes just going well with things touched by the essence of the Underworld)<br /> <br /> The Incarnae while mysterious and sometimes distant are undeniably still puisant, present and active in Creation's affairs - but how loud is the fall of a tree where nothing exists to hear it? Are the Dark Mother, the Elemental Dragons or Ketu less truly puisant than the UCS, Luna or the Maidens or just more elusive &amp; idiosyncratic on the peculiar priorities in the making of their Chosen? The same principle might be said to apply with any &quot;lesser&quot; Incarna patrons. More obscure/secretive does not exactly have to mean weaker.<br /> <br /> As an aside, i've toyed with the idea of Uranus, Neptune &amp; Pluto as either fallen Maidens - or copycats/impostors entities <b>claiming</b> to be so - in a few past games of my own, among a few other things relating to [alleged] dead Incarnae.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure I understand the criticism? Like, yeah, I started by focusing on Magical Materials, and derived the metaphysical system from them. Given that assumption, I had to add a form of Exalts which are Celestials, but by doing so I would have had to also add their patrons. Doing so would have inflated the number of the Incrana to a high degree, so I decided to create a sub-category called &quot;Lesser Incrana&quot;, and then I had to define what makes them &quot;lesser&quot;. If you have issue with naming those ascended gods as &quot;lesser&quot;, well, I guess it is a matter of personal preference? If it is about it being a &quot;self produced problem&quot;, well, yeah, it is, as again I started from which MM I wanted and built the system from there.<br /> <br /> So.. yeah, this is what it is. I personally like the concept so I don't see it much of a &quot;problem&quot; anymore, but to each their own I guess?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}